ell trails badly in fundraising with minimal cash on hand"], "rationale": "The fundamentals point strongly Democratic: a D+11 seat, an entrenched incumbent, and a September UNH poll showing a 22-point lead. Russell's fundraising disadvantage and market pricing near 96% for Pingree confirm Safe D status.", "watch": "A major late-breaking shift in the national environment or a strong Russell debate performance could narrow the margin, though not enough to threaten the seat.", "confidence": "high", "notes": ["No expert rater lists this race; treated as safe for the party holding the seat.", "Incumbent Chellie Pingree (D) is running."]}, "overview": "Chellie Pingree is seeking a 10th term in a Portland-area district that leans Democratic by about 11 points. She enters the general election with a large financial advantage over Republican Ronald Russell, an Army veteran who won his primary in June but has raised modest sums and holds little cash. The two have met in debates and candidate forums through October.\n\nA late-September University of New Hampshire poll of likely voters showed Pingree ahead 57 to 35, and prediction markets price her chances near 96 percent. With no outside spending targeting the race and no expert ratings flagging it as competitive, the evidence consistently points to a comfortable incumbent win.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.989, "margin": 20.81}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.9938, "margin": 20.5}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.9879, "margin": 20.9}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.9946, "margin": 21.5}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.9957, "margin": 21.5}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.995, "margin": 21.5}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.9949, "margin": 21.5}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.9958, "margin": 21.5}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.9948, "margin": 21.5}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.9951, "margin": 21.5}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.9978, "margin": 21.5}, {"date": "2026-10-03"